# Competition benchmark files and build artifacts
/*.ps1
/build/**/*.z
*.c
# batch 340: `*.c` is a bare extension and it sits in a block whose stated intent is
# "competition benchmark files and build artifacts". Measured: exactly ONE file in the
# repo depends on this rule today -- runtime/aliases.inc.c, which is @generated
# (tools/gen_from_registry.py --emit-aliases) and #included by runtime/tokio_runtime_stub.c:358.
# Naming it instead of the extension keeps that file ignored and stops swallowing any
# hand-written .c a future batch adds to runtime/.
!*.c
runtime/aliases.inc.c
*.a
*.lib
*.exp
/competition_*
/murphy_*
# batch 346: `zeta_*` was deleted from this line -- it swallowed the zeta_src/ self-host
/test_*
# batch 340: `*.z` (above -- since 346 it is `/build/**/*.z`) and this `test_*` (since
# together they swallowed THREE hand-written sources. Measured by moving two of them
# aside for a single run: python_style went 291 passed / 2 failed -> 287 / 5, because the
# compiler loads pylib/numpy.z at runtime (t212/t227/t230 turn red) and t124_ternary
# vanished from the count entirely. A green gate was resting on files that are NOT in
# the repository -- same debt as `run_*` swallowing tools/run_all.sh (batch 314 above).
# Artifact side untouched: build/stubs/**/*.z and root-level test_*.z stay ignored.
!pylib/*.z
!tests/**/*.z
/build_*
/run_*
# batch 314: ci.yml "baselines" job runs ./tools/run_all.sh (ci.yml:106), but the
# `run_*` rule above also swallows it -> the file was never tracked, so that CI step
# could only ever fail. Re-include this one path; keep `run_*` for root scratch.
!tools/run_all.sh
/simple_*
/final_*
competition/**/*.rs
competition_submission/**/*.rs

# Performance reports and algorithm documentation
*_WHEEL_DELIVERABLE.md
PERFORMANCE_*.md
# batch 345: line 153 used to read `PERFORMANCE_*.md` + `z\x00e\x00t\x00a\x00/\x00` -- a
# UTF-16-mangled `zeta/` rule. Deliberately NOT restored: tests/zeta/ holds 10 tracked
# hand-written .z test sources, and a bare directory rule would swallow every new file
# added there (same root as batches 314/340). `zeta_*` above still covers root scratch.

